    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This podcast focus on the personal stories of three individuals. The first story is about the calming factors that the sound of water has, and also how sound can change our moods. The second story is about non-traditional students, and how they have pursued education later in their lives. The focus is on their personal experiences and how this shapes them as students. The third story focuses on the identity of a member of the Stanford marching band. The role that an individual plays in a community is highlighted. Thematically the three are connected with the notion of transformation.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
